 # Fourier Features Mapping
 
-Also called: Fourier Features, FFM, RFF Encoding, Random Fourier Features (RFF) Encoding
+Also called: FFM, Fourier Features, RFF Encoding, Random Fourier Features (RFF) Encoding
 
 ## Overview
-Fourier Features Mapping (FFM) is a preprocessing technique that transforms low-dimensional input coordinates into a higher-dimensional space using sinusoidal functions to overcome the spectral bias of vanilla Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLPs) [S1][S3, unofficial][S4]. It enables the network to learn high-frequency details early and fast by transforming the effective Neural Tangent Kernel (NTK) into a stationary kernel with a tunable bandwidth [S2][S4]. Unlike coordinate-based geometric approaches, FFM decouples the neural architecture from the spatial representation, allowing flexible integration into implicit neural representations [S1].
+Fourier Features Mapping (FFM) is a preprocessing technique that transforms low-dimensional input coordinates into a higher-dimensional space using sinusoidal functions to overcome the spectral bias of vanilla Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLPs) [S1][S5, unofficial]. It enables the network to learn high-frequency details early and fast by transforming the effective Neural Tangent Kernel (NTK) into a stationary kernel with a tunable bandwidth [S5, unofficial]. Unlike coordinate-based geometric approaches, FFM decouples the neural architecture from the spatial representation, allowing flexible integration into implicit neural representations [S1].
 
