 ## Background
-*   **Origin:** Introduced by Tancik et al. (2020) for implicit neural representations [S1][S3, unofficial].
-*   **History:** Based on the random Fourier feature mapping originally proposed by Rahimi & Recht (2007) [S3, unofficial].
-*   **Development:** Initially proposed to overcome the spectral bias of vanilla MLPs, which fail to capture high-frequency details even with deep and wide networks [S1]. It was shown that passing inputs through FFM transforms the effective NTK into a stationary kernel [S2][S4].
+*   **Origin:** Introduced by Tancik et al. (2020) for implicit neural representations [S1][S5, unofficial].
+*   **History:** Based on the random Fourier feature mapping originally proposed by Rahimi & Recht (2007) [S5, unofficial].
+*   **Development:** Initially proposed to overcome the spectral bias of vanilla MLPs, which fail to capture high-frequency details even with deep and wide networks [S1]. It was shown that passing inputs through FFM transforms the effective NTK into a stationary kernel [S4].
 *   **Usage:** Applied in Neural Fields / Implicit Neural Representations to condition MLPs on spatial coordinates. Used for image superresolution, denoising, inpainting, video generation, and 3D content rendering [S5, unofficial]. Also used in frameworks like NeuralVDB to decouple network design from VDB tree structure [S1].
 
